      coBody: "The check-in page's colour theme is a single platform-wide setting, identical for every warehouse — there is no per-organisation colour picker. The browser tab stays ours too: it reads QRGo Driver, with our icon, even on your own domain. We would rather say both of those here than let you find them after signing. What is genuinely yours is the part drivers actually read: your logo, your cover photo, your name and address, your contact details, your hours, and your domain in the address bar.",
      faqTitle: "Questions buyers ask about white-label",
      q1: "Can I set my own brand colours on the check-in page?",
      a1: "No. The check-in page uses one platform-wide colour theme, the same for every warehouse, and there is no per-organisation colour picker. Your brand colour reaches the page through the two images you control: the logo at the top and the cover photo behind it. Everything else — name, address, contact, hours, domain — is yours to set.",
      q2: "Does the check-in page really run on my own domain?",
      a2: "Yes. Enter a domain you own, such as checkin.example.com, add the CNAME or A record the dashboard shows you at your DNS provider, then press Verify Domain. Once it verifies, drivers reach your check-in page over HTTPS at your address. One domain per warehouse, and qrgo.ro/your-slug keeps working alongside it.",
      q3: "How long does the domain take to go live?",
      a3: "That depends on your DNS provider, not on Logistiq. The dashboard notes that DNS changes can take up to 48 hours to propagate, and you can press Verify Domain as often as you like. Until it verifies, the domain redirects to qrgo.ro and your check-in page keeps running at qrgo.ro/your-slug throughout.",
      q4: "Does white-label cover the mobile app and the dashboard too?",
      a4: "Partly, and it is worth being precise. Your logo and cover photo appear on the driver check-in page and inside the QRGo Driver app, next to your warehouse name. The app is published in the stores as QRGo Driver, the browser tab on your check-in page reads QRGo Driver with our icon — even on your own domain — and the dashboard your dispatchers use stays Logistiq. What carries your brand is the body of the driver-facing page: your images, your details, your address bar.",
