      faqTitle: "Frequently asked questions about driver instructions",
      q1: "How does the instruction reach the driver?",
      a1: "It appears on the check-in status page at qrgo.ro. The page holds a realtime connection, so the driver watches the card change the moment you press send — no refresh, no polling — and a localized push notification goes out in parallel. These instructions are not sent by SMS.",
      q2: "Is the message I type translated for the driver?",
      a2: "No. Only the fixed wording is translated — \"What to do\", \"Please come to the office\", \"Go to parking\" — into twelve languages, picked by the driver's own language choice. Anything you type yourself, including ramp instructions, arrives exactly as written. With mixed fleets, the action type and the card colour carry the meaning on their own.",
      q3: "What happens when the wait time runs out?",
      a3: "The countdown recomputes every minute and shows the hours and minutes left, plus an estimated time for loading or unloading. At zero the card switches to your expiration message, or to the default: \"The waiting time has passed, you will immediately receive the next instruction.\" The estimated time is optional — leave it out and the driver simply sees your message.",
      q4: "Can a driver confirm or reply to an instruction?",
      a4: "Not on the instruction card — it shows one thing, the next step, with no reply button and no read receipt. Conversation belongs to the separate check-in chat, where driver and dispatcher can write to each other. There is only ever one card: a new action replaces the old one, and Call to Office always takes priority.",
