      specTitle: "Four instructions on the driver's screen",
      specSub: "A dispatcher picks one instruction from the check-in Actions menu. Each becomes a colour-coded card on the driver's status page. Fixed wording shows in the driver's language; a note the dispatcher types appears exactly as written.",
      k1: "Wait — amber",
      v1: "An amber card. With an ETA set, the driver sees a countdown (\"You need to wait 25 minutes\") and the estimated time for unloading, refreshed each minute. When it runs out, the dispatcher's expiry note takes over. Without an ETA, only the wait message shows.",
      k2: "Call to Office — blue",
      v2: "A blue card reading \"Please come to the office\". It takes priority in the driver's main \"What to do\" card, while the separate \"Assigned Ramp\" card — photo, instructions, Open in Maps — stays on screen.",
      k3: "Send to Parking — teal",
      v3: "A teal card naming the exact bay the dispatcher chose — \"Go to parking: [Parcare Nord] A12\" — built from the parking and spot names.",
      k4: "Other Action — orange",
      v4: "An orange card whose headline is the dispatcher's free text, shown exactly as typed. A plain written instruction — no template, no reply field.",
      k5: "Assigned Ramp — green",
      v5: "A green card \"Go to Rampa 3\", plus a separate \"Assigned Ramp\" card carrying the ramp photo, written instructions, and an \"Open in Maps\" button to the ramp's coordinates (shown when coordinates are set).",
      k6: "Live delivery",
      v6: "Every instruction lands on the driver's status page the moment it is sent, over a live realtime channel — no refresh and no SMS. A localized push notification goes out alongside it.",
