      coKind: "roadmap",
      coTitle: "QRGoBox is in progress, and we say so",
      coBody: "Built today: the gate scanner device, which validates the check-in, and the gate log, with every scan by a registered gate device and its outcome. In progress: QRGoBox and manual opening from logistiq.cloud, whose command to the barrier will go out only over a secure connection (TLS), which we are preparing now. The QRGoBox hardware and software versions are in beta and are currently being tested. If you want a barrier on your yard opened by your check-ins, talk to us.",
      faqTitle: "Questions worth asking before you wire a barrier",
      q1: "Does the QRGoBox scan the QR code?",
      a1: "No. The gate scanner device reads the driver's QR and the platform checks the check-in; QRGoBox will only receive the command to open the barrier. Every decision is made on the platform, never on the box.",
      q2: "Does a valid scan open the barrier today?",
      a2: "Not yet. Today the scanner validates the check-in, and every scan by a registered gate device is written to the gate access log with its outcome, but no barrier opens from Logistiq: QRGoBox and the secure connection for its command are in progress. Until then, a valid scan tells the driver that the barrier did not respond and to contact the operator.",
      q3: "Which check-ins will the gate let through?",
      a3: "At the entry, only those confirmed, assigned or under way: a driver still waiting for a dispatcher to confirm is turned away, and the refusal is stored with its reason. At the exit, a completed visit leaves once, on the day it was completed or within the hour after it. The scanner applies these rules today, and the barrier will follow them once QRGoBox is ready.",
